# S3 — learning rate of each downstream arm (rriva, 2026-10-26). Three learning
# rates a factor 2 apart around the sqrt-B prior of S1, lr(B) = 3e-4 * sqrt(B / 2048)
# (Adam: the gradient noise falls as 1/sqrt(B), so the step that keeps the same
# signal-to-noise grows as sqrt(B)). One seed (42), on the seed-42 pretrainings
# (P_full, QK-norm, 30 epochs, last.ckpt); campaign defaults: 40-epoch cosine,
# early stopping on val CE (patience 12), QK-norm. JC weight 0.3, lambda 0.4.
# FT also with the pretrained parts at lr / 10 (backbone_lr). P2 has no
# downstream arm for now (rriva, 2026-10-26).
#
# Batch per arm fills ~92% of the 45 GiB card (rriva: fill the card, frozen arms
# included), scaled from the memory measured on the first S3 launch
# (S3_lr_20261026_095940_ABORTED_smallbatch) and the S2_qk probes; the batch
# only has to be a multiple of chunk_size (512):
#   SC / FT      35.3 GiB at 24576 -> 28672   lr centre 1.12e-3
#   + JC         34.6 GiB at 12288 -> 14336   lr centre 7.9e-4
#   frozen       14.2 GiB at 32768 -> 94208   lr centre 2.0e-3  (~200 steps/epoch)
#   frozen + JC  53760 from S0's frozen / frozen + JC memory ratio (not measured)
# Host RAM: the frozen arm at 94208 was killed at 22 GB per GPU (data-loader
# prefetch of 12 batches of ~0.4 GB each): its cells and the P1 arms run with
# MEM_PER_GPU_GB=40.
# FR <- P0 at 94208 then went NaN in its first epoch (S3_lr_20261027_093035_ABORTED_varlen):
# flash varlen's backward overflowed its 32-bit-indexed dq buffer at >62k aggregator
# sequences; fixed in 3a22662 (launches sliced under 2**31 elements), then rerun.
# S3 result (2026-10-27): FT <- P0 is better with the pretrained parts at lr / 10
# (0.630 vs 0.644), so FT <- P1 + JC uses backbone_lr = lr / 10.
# Epoch on an A40: SC ~20 min, + JC ~2x, frozen ~9 min.
#
# Now (P0 is done), longest cells first:
#   ENCODERS=rowcol_concat_v0 CHUNK=512 SEEDS=42 PACKS=4 MEM_PER_GPU_GB=22 \
#   MAX_EPOCHS=40 EST_SECONDS_PER_EPOCH=1250 WALLTIME=2-00:00:00 \
#   CELL_FILTER='^(sc|scjc|ft_p0|fr_p0)_' CELLS=scripts/configs/campaign/S3_lr.cells bash slurm/ssl_pack.sh
# The P1 arms only once the P1 pretraining (P_full_20261026_094445) has completed
# or with DEPENDENCY=afterany:<its pack>: a cell on a pretraining that is not
# completed is skipped as failed. FT + JC takes the backbone_lr that wins FT <- P0.
#   ... CELL_FILTER='_p1_' ...
scjc_lr4e-4  arm=scratch finetune.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=0.3 encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=14336 optimizer.lr=4e-4 @est=2500
scjc_lr8e-4  arm=scratch finetune.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=0.3 encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=14336 optimizer.lr=8e-4 @est=2500
scjc_lr1.6e-3  arm=scratch finetune.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=0.3 encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=14336 optimizer.lr=1.6e-3 @est=2500
sc_lr5.6e-4  arm=scratch encoders=${ENCODERS} chunk_size=${CHUNK} datamodule.batch_size=28672 optimizer.lr=5.6e-4
